libssc: skip the python mock server when building the Nabu stack

The mocking/ subdirectory unconditionally requires a python dependency via
meson's python module (python.dependency()), which is only available natively
and is not needed for the Nabu runtime: the mock server is used by libssc's own
test suite only.  The tests/ subdirectory merely refers to its path as a string
for exe_wrapper, so dropping the subdir keeps configure/compile working.

--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -101,7 +101,6 @@
 headers = files()
 map_source = files('libssc.map')
 
-subdir('mocking')
 subdir('data')
 subdir('src')
 subdir('tests')
